Creating Methods Inside Objects
A method is simply a function inside an object.

js
Copy
Edit
const user = {
  name: "John",
  greet: function() {
    console.log("Hello!");
  }
};

user.greet(); // Output: "Hello!"
✅ You can also use shorthand syntax:

js
Copy
Edit
const user = {
  name: "John",
  greet() {
    console.log("Hello!");
  }
};
🔹 2. Using the this Keyword
this refers to the object the method is called on.

js
Copy
Edit
const user = {
  name: "John",
  greet() {
    console.log(`Hi, I'm ${this.name}`);
  }
};

user.greet(); // Output: "Hi, I'm John"
Why use this?
Allows the method to access other properties of the same object.

Keeps your code flexible if the object name changes.

🔸 Important Notes
❗ this depends on how the function is called, not where it’s defined.
js
Copy
Edit
const user = {
  name: "Alice",
  greet() {
    console.log(this.name);
  }
};

const sayHi = user.greet;
sayHi(); // Output: undefined (or error in strict mode)